---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const p='/equipment/13-15/';
const index='https://www.embl.org/groups/electron-microscopy-core-facility/equipment/';
const primary='https://www.embl.org/groups/electron-microscopy-core-facility/bruker-skyscan-1272-microct/';
const photo='https://www.embl.org/groups/electron-microscopy-core-facility/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/microCT-1024x768.jpg';
const dims='https://tecnasa.es/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/microCT-SKYSCAN-1272-CMOS.pdf#page=12';
const maker='https://www.bruker.com/en/products-and-solutions/diffractometers-and-x-ray-microscopes/3d-x-ray-microscopes.html';
const refs=[
 ['front.webp','Front view: white wing shells, central dark shielded door, side supports and visible 1272 identification.',photo,'EMBL front photograph'],
 ['quarter.webp','Right-front view: width, height, side supports and footprint; rear surfaces are inferred.',dims,'Bruker drawing T118603, PDF p. 12']
];
const checks=[
 ['Slice 8 height','1.60 mm','1.60 mm','1 nm (arithmetic only)'],
 ['Two-bead center separation at slice 8','2.60 mm','2.60 mm','1 nm (arithmetic only)'],
 ['Missing saved slice 6','Missing, no distance','Missing, no distance','Exact'],
 ['Stored slice 0','Stored, no distance','Stored, no distance','Exact'],
 ['Exterior W × D × H','1,160 × 520 × 330 mm','1,160 × 520 × 330 mm','0.1 mm (geometric)']
];
---
<Layout title="SkyScan 1272 · Passive micro-CT slice exhibit" description="Documentary exterior and passive slices of a fully synthetic inert two-bead geometry. No scanner control or reconstruction.">
 <main id="sky15">
  <p><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-15/">← Equipment record 13-15</a></p>
  <p class="series">LABORATORY EQUIPMENT / 13-15 / READ-ONLY EXHIBIT</p>
  <h1>SkyScan 1272 Micro-CT</h1>
  <p class="lead">Inspect the closed Bruker enclosure and step through a separate archive of an inert two-bead phantom. The ruler measures the distance between the centers of the two labeled shapes in a saved slice. There is no scanner operation or specimen workflow.</p>
  <div class="duo">
   <section class="card">
    <h2>Documentary enclosure</h2>
    <div id="sky-view" class="viewer"></div><p id="sky-model" role="status">Loading metric 3D model…</p>
    <div class="actions" aria-label="3D viewpoints">
     <button type="button" data-sky-view="orbit">Reset orbit</button><button type="button" data-sky-view="front">Front</button><button type="button" data-sky-view="side">Right flank</button><button type="button" data-sky-view="archive">Detached exhibit</button>
    </div>
    <p>Drag to orbit and scroll or pinch to zoom. Tap the detached exhibit screen to advance by one saved-plane index. The enclosure has no actions.</p>
   </section>
   <section class="card">
    <h2>Read-only inert slice ruler</h2>
    <canvas id="sky-raster" width="480" height="440" aria-label="Fixed synthetic labeled slice with a two-bead ruler and 1 mm scale."></canvas>
    <div class="inputs"><label for="sky-index">Plane index <span id="sky-index-value">8</span><input id="sky-index" type="range" min="0" max="16" step="1" value="8"/></label></div>
    <div class="actions"><button id="sky-next" type="button" disabled>Next plane</button><button id="sky-missing" type="button">Show missing plane</button><button id="sky-reset" type="button">Center plane</button><button id="sky-export" type="button" disabled>Export ruler JSON</button></div>
    <p id="sky-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading fixed geometric slices…</p>
    <p id="sky-plane" class="readout"></p><p id="sky-result" class="readout"></p>
   </section>
  </div>
  <section>
   <h2>Configuration and illustrated references</h2>
   <p>The register previously said <strong>1270</strong>, matching the label in the <a href={index}>EMBL accessory index</a>. That exact entry links to <a href={primary}>EMBL's 1272 instrument page</a>; the installed unit's front badge reads <strong>1272</strong>, and <a href={maker}>Bruker identifies the 1272 series</a>. Record ID <strong>13-15</strong> is unchanged. This model depicts the publicly documented standard <strong>SkyScan 1272 CMOS Edition</strong> exterior without the optional changer. The EMBL image corroborates the 1272 chassis and identity, not the exact internal detector generation at that site.</p>
   <div class="refs">
    {refs.map(([f,label,href,source])=><figure><img src={p+f} alt={label} width="780" height="500" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Original reference-based rendering.</strong> {label} <a href={href}>{source} (original)</a>.</figcaption></figure>)}
   </div>
   <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Value</th><th>Source / role</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Cabinet W × D × H</td><td>1,160 × 520 × 330 mm, standard version</td><td><a href={dims}>Bruker T118603, p. 12</a>. Axis assignment follows the Front/Right dimension arrows; optional changer intentionally omitted.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Face detail and shape</td><td>Publicly visible shielded door, central recess, body trim and support pylons</td><td><a href={photo}>EMBL photo</a>; small details and unknown rear geometry estimated, no measured CAD.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Phantom spacing</td><td>0.10 × 0.10 × 0.20 mm per voxel</td><td><a href={p+'phantom.json'}>Synthetic label stack</a>. Not Bruker spatial resolution or a measured calibration.</td></tr>
   </tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section>
   <h2>What the ruler measures</h2>
   <p>Each saved plane is a row-major array of two discrete sphere labels and background, not attenuation or CT intensity. The coordinate origin is the first voxel center; column increases right, row increases down, and plane index increases with Z. Average the in-plane positions of each bead's labeled voxels to find that plane's centroids, then take the Euclidean distance between them. Plane 8 contains both intended centers, independently spaced at (24 × 0.10, 10 × 0.10) mm apart, or 2.60 mm.</p>
   <p>Plane 6 is deliberately absent and is not interpolated. A stored plane without two labels has no distance either. The JSON result retains sample and plane IDs, revision, coverage, spacing, bead centers and the computed distance if present. This is a direct replay of ideal synthetic geometry. It does not acquire images, model imaging physics, or reconstruct missing data. No scanner control, specimen handling or immersive verification is included.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
   <h2>Focused verification</h2>
   <div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Test</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(([name,x,y,t])=><tr><td>{name}</td><td>{x}</td><td>{y}</td><td>{t}</td><td>Pass</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
   <p><a href={p+'verification.json'}>Verification results</a> · <a href={p+'contract.json'}>Input/output contract</a> · <a href={p+'example-ruler.json'}>Example result</a> · <a href={p+'phantom.json'}>Fixed phantom</a> · <a href={p+'build-fixture.py'}>Fixture source</a></p>
   <p><a href={p+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={p+'skyscan1272.glb'} download>Download metric GLB</a> · <a href={p+'interaction.json'}>Interaction manifest</a> · <a href={p+'asset-metrics.json'}>GLB metrics</a></p>
  </section>
 </main>
</Layout>
<script>
import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-15/client.mjs';
</script>
<style>
main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:1.2rem clamp(.9rem,2.5vw,2rem) 3rem}
.series,.readout,table,input,select,button{font-family:var(--font-label,system-ui,sans-serif)}
.series{font-size:.78rem;letter-spacing:.13em}.lead{max-width:72ch}
.duo,.refs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.2rem 0}
.card{border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 30%,transparent);padding:1rem;border-radius:.25rem}
.viewer{height:clamp(23rem,45vw,32rem);overflow:hidden;background:#263949}
.viewer :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%;touch-action:none}
#sky-raster{display:block;width:min(100%,26rem);height:auto;background:#263949;margin:.5rem auto 1rem}
.actions,.inputs{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.6rem 0}
button,input,select{background:transparent;color:inherit;border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 50%,transparent);border-radius:.2rem;padding:.5rem;font-size:.91rem;min-height:2.6rem}
button{cursor:pointer}button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:not-allowed}input{width:min(18rem,55vw)}label{display:grid;font-size:.86rem;gap:.25rem}
figure{margin:0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}figcaption{font-size:.92rem;margin:.45rem 0}
section{margin:1.5rem 0}.duo section{margin:0}
.tablewrap{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.88rem}td,th{border-bottom:1px solid color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 25%,transparent);text-align:left;padding:.5rem;vertical-align:top}
[data-error=true]{font-weight:bold;color:var(--accent,currentColor)}
@media(max-width:770px){.duo,.refs{grid-template-columns:1fr}.viewer{height:22rem}}
</style>
